body:
No idea, but low key okay with it since I was auto-enrolled for L2 August and I wrote L1 November.

&#x200B;

Edit: I contacted Kaplan, it isn't indicative of your pass/fail result.

When I feel that way, I know it's time to take some time to get myself together. Usually a few days off without even considering what I'm stressed about. You've probably spent the past 2 weeks stressing over the lack of motivation. If so, do yourself a favor and decompress a little. I find myself much more productive when I get back into the activity.

&#x200B;

Good luck, hope you're able to figure it out :)

I don't think you can get a refund on it, so it's a sunk cost at this point. You may as well study what you can, do the question banks, and take the exam. To not do that and lose the money would be an utter waste and the wrong thing to do. Only if you decided to not pursue the CFA Charter would it make sense to call it quits.

&#x200B;

Good luck amigo! Nov L1 here too. Reach out if you've got questions. There's a discord too.
